# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS

`st-wl-copy` [<WL-COPY-OPTION>...]

## DESCRIPTION

st-wl-copy is a drop-in replacement for `wl-copy`(1) (Wayland) that filters
standard input through `sclip`(1) before it is placed on the clipboard. Every
argument is forwarded verbatim to `wl-copy`, so native options such as
`--primary` or `--trim-newline` work unchanged.

By default the strip is strictest (printable ASCII only). Set the environment
variable `SCLIP_MODE=unicode` to keep printable non-ASCII instead.

## ENVIRONMENT

  * `SCLIP_MODE`:
    When set to `unicode`, keep printable non-ASCII (passes `--unicode` to
    `sclip`). Any other value (or unset) is the default ASCII-only strip.

## EXIT STATUS

The exit status of the underlying `sclip` | `wl-copy` pipeline; 127 if `wl-copy`
is not installed.

## SEE ALSO

`st-wl-paste`(1), `st-xclip`(1), `sclip`(1), `wl-copy`(1)
